    "body": "### Problem\r\n\r\nWhen repeating a visual operation via `.` (e.g. `<C-v>jI1<Esc>`), a failed motion like `j` on the last line calls `clearopbeep()`, which calls `beep_flush()`. `beep_flush()` calls `flush_buffers(FLUSH_MINIMAL)` and clears the stuffed redo buffer, discarding the pending operator keys (`I1<Esc>`) and leaving Neovim stuck in Visual mode.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\n\r\nKeep flushing on errors to preserve map-error. When flush_buffers() discards pending redo keys, also end Visual mode. This covers both failed motions that beep and errors such as jumping to an unset mark.\r\n\r\nFixes #41896",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-30T14:16:28Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the help!\r\n\r\nAI findings:\r\n- breaks `:h map-error` (macros like `Vjd@q` won't stop at a failed motion).\r\n  - Suggested fix: keep flushing, and have `flush_buffers()` also call `end_visual_mode()` when it throws away pending redo keys (`readbuf2` not empty) while Visual mode is active.\r\n    - Because it lives in `flush_buffers()`, not `beep_flush()`, it also covers failures that raise an error rather than a beep. `emsg()` calls flush_buffers() directly, e.g. E20 when the replayed selection jumps to an unset mark.\r\n",
